# PROPOSAL — NOT APPLIED.  DO NOT auto-apply / auto-deploy.
#
# Audit finding H1: life-safety Telegram alerts call `notify.send_message` with an
# `inline_keyboard` in the service data.  The telegram_bot integration's notify
# ENTITY (`notify.send_message`) schema only accepts `message` + `title`, so the
# extra `inline_keyboard` key is rejected — the call returns HTTP 400 Bad Request
# and NO message is delivered at all (proven live 2026-07-15: notify+inline_keyboard
# => 400; telegram_bot.send_message+inline_keyboard => 200).
#
# Fix: convert each affected block from
#     action: notify.send_message  (target: entity_id: notify.…; data:)
# to  action: telegram_bot.send_message  (data: chat_id: 100000000)
# keeping the same `message` and the same `inline_keyboard` list-of-lists shape
# [[["Label","/cb"]]] — which telegram_bot.send_message DOES accept and render.
# Every callback_data (/leak_confirm, /moisture_false_alarm, /siren_off,
# /security_disarm) already has a handler in automation 1778700001005, so no
# handler changes are required.
#
# Target file on HA: /config/automations.yaml
# 8 blocks across 5 automations:
#   1748000001001 "Утечка воды v4"           (2 blocks)  — ENABLED
#   1775638334800 "Утечка воды v2"           (2 blocks)  — DISABLED (initial_state:false); convert for consistency
#   1778700001005 "Telegram обработчик кнопок" (2 blocks) — ENABLED
#   1779200002001 "Задымление — сирена"       (1 block)   — ENABLED
#   1779200003001 "Охрана — тревога"          (1 block)   — ENABLED
#
# Line numbers below reflect the audited copy of /config/automations.yaml
# (4106 lines, fetched 2026-07-15). Apply with context/fuzz, then validate YAML +
# `automation.reload` in a maintenance window.  See TELEGRAM_SAFETY.md deploy plan.
